<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<opml version="2.0" xmlns:porridge="https://github.com/alexjj/porridge">
  <head>
    <title>2026</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <outline text="November 2026" type="calendarMonth" date="2026-11">
      <outline text="26th November" type="calendarDay" date="2026-11-26">
        <outline text="![Happy Thanksgiving 🦃](/images/2026/11/x10f6199-26202506.webp)" created="Thu, 26 Nov 2026 20:19:55 GMT"/>
        <outline text="That photo was taken with my X100F back in 2019. Looking at the other photos with the X100F isn't helping my urge for the X100VI..." created="Thu, 26 Nov 2026 20:25:09 GMT"/>
        <outline text="Porridge Updates 🥣" created="Thu, 26 Nov 2026 20:26:16 GMT">
          <outline text="Under the settings you can add external links to the navbar. You can also reorder everything, but the order is still retained in the individual page's settings. So if you move stuff about, that's why the pages will be highlighted as changed. Not sure if that's useful or not but there we go." created="Thu, 26 Nov 2026 20:26:36 GMT"/>
          <outline text="Pick a favicon from an emoji! 🥁 Choose yours under the settings page."/>
        </outline>
      </outline>
      <outline text="25th November" type="calendarDay" date="2026-11-25">
        <outline text="![Hobonichi delivery!](/images/2026/11/img-5592-25155303.jpg)" created="Wed, 25 Nov 2026 15:52:17 GMT"/>
        <outline text="I need a practice notebook to make sure I don't mess up the real one. 😅 This sounds dumb, but I want to use it how I want to use it, not how other people use theirs...but I still can't help looking for &quot;good ideas&quot;." created="Wed, 25 Nov 2026 15:53:07 GMT"/>
        <outline text="I've stopped after a couple of videos, things turn into super complex systems and I don't need that. I do like folding a page in half, then making a 2.5 page spread with info in the middle. Anyway, I've started a list of what I want to include and then figure out how I'm going to do it. It officially starts on the 30th November, so I've got a few days to get comfortable in it. No idea what to use some of the built in lists but I'm going to use the 365 tracker to track using the notebook itself! I'm glad I've got the memo books, as I can use those and avoid the &quot;*fear of doing it wrong*&quot;, as I can just write whatever in those and then when they get used up move onto another, or if something is really good bring it into the main Weeks notebook." created="Wed, 25 Nov 2026 21:45:32 GMT"/>
        <outline text="The Capless Pilot is really nice too. Like the fine nib, although the ink needs 20-30 seconds to be dry, so don't close the page immediately. Perhaps a huge bottle of ink was a bit much and maybe I should've bought a selection of cartridges to figure out what's best. It's fine though." created="Wed, 25 Nov 2026 21:48:59 GMT"/>
        <outline text="I think I want to bring it to work with me, although not sure exactly what for, but I should have it with me and also to use the pen. This makes me think I need some bag to bring and back and forth, one that's suitable cycling but not a rucksack as that's unnecessarily big. Maybe some sling? Have to look into that." created="Wed, 25 Nov 2026 21:50:10 GMT"/>
        <outline text="Earthbound" created="Wed, 25 Nov 2026 21:53:39 GMT">
          <outline text="![Earthbound screenshot](/images/2026/11/image-25215402.png)" created="Wed, 25 Nov 2026 21:53:42 GMT"/>
          <outline text="I picked my Weeks as it was the cheapest in the sale. I've since realised that it's a retro Nintendo game called [Mother](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mother_(video_game_series%29)) (in Japan) and Earthbound everywhere else. This is where Ness is from, plus it looks like an interesting RPG. I'm going to have to play it, at least for an hour or two." created="Wed, 25 Nov 2026 21:51:43 GMT"/>
        </outline>
        <outline text="I've been wondering about making importer for Porridge. e.g. from micro.blog, or general markdown files. My effort in doing it isn't much, ask Claude and explain a few things, and wait. What I'm mostly thinking about is what do I actually want to import, everything? a selection? But does it really matter?" created="Wed, 25 Nov 2026 19:51:35 GMT"/>
        <outline text="I've been reading Charlotte's Web to my youngest. There's a certain style of writing of children's books from that era. I quite like it, and miss it in newer books. Old fashioned way of speaking, and things grandparents would say? *This is an awfully good meal mother; I really can't abide the Smith's new television.* I've found the [1973 cartoon movie](https://www.imdb.com/title/tt0070016/) of it for us to watch once we finish too." created="Wed, 25 Nov 2026 21:56:13 GMT"/>
        <outline text="Making notebooks" created="Wed, 25 Nov 2026 21:42:20 GMT">
          <outline text="Something on my todo is making notebooks... reddit pointed me to this video"/>
          <outline text="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0984uZFc5bw" created="Wed, 25 Nov 2026 21:43:12 GMT"/>
        </outline>
      </outline>
      <outline text="24th November" type="calendarDay" date="2026-11-24">
        <outline text="![Dusting of snow](/images/2026/11/img-5582-24200239.jpg)" created="Tue, 24 Nov 2026 20:01:45 GMT"/>
        <outline text="It was cold out today. Think I could do with a sit mat now. Sitting on the ground for half an hour made my legs go numb, luckily there was no one around to watch me try and stand up!" created="Tue, 24 Nov 2026 20:02:43 GMT"/>
        <outline text="I forget about Dropbox, even though it's stood the test of time. I have about 20-odd GB of space on my free account from various ancient promos. It does nag me incessantly to upgrade though. " created="Tue, 24 Nov 2026 20:09:46 GMT"/>
        <outline text="I seem to have a whole load of admin when I return from doing SOTA activations, including:" created="Tue, 24 Nov 2026 20:37:14 GMT" list="bullets">
          <outline text="Uploading logs to SOTA and POTA (although usually do that whilst walking back to the car)" created="Tue, 24 Nov 2026 20:37:30 GMT"/>
          <outline text="Add route to sotamaps, if it doesn't exist (usually doesn't in Scotland)"/>
          <outline text="Edit photos (press auto on my phone for each one) and transfer to computer - usually via Dropbox as it renames them all as well"/>
          <outline text="Add photos to sotlas"/>
          <outline text="Download gpx tracks from Garmin Connect"/>
          <outline text="Make a new blog post on &lt;gm5alx.uk&gt;, which is now very easy with my site manager, and just requires dragging and dropping the logs, the gpx and the photos for a &quot;basic&quot; post. Writing is optional."/>
          <outline text="Tick it off my sota planner app"/>
          <outline text="If it's worthwhile I'll write up a trip report on the [SOTA forums](https://reflector.sota.org.uk), then maybe later copy that to my blog."/>
          <outline text="Oh and there's the video footage to download, edit, make a thumbnail, upload to YouTube"/>
          <outline text="Maybe post to some socials? Perhaps a picture to [OARC](https://www.oarc.uk/) discord or mastodon.radio. 😮‍💨"/>
        </outline>
        <outline text="Porridge updates 🥣" list="bullets" created="Tue, 24 Nov 2026 20:43:23 GMT">
          <outline text="Normalised capitalisation for [Phil](https://twelvety.github.io/porridge-blog/). " created="Tue, 24 Nov 2026 20:43:31 GMT"/>
          <outline text="Not done yet but figuring out the editor on iOS and keyboard things that pop up."/>
        </outline>
      </outline>
      <outline text="23rd November" type="calendarDay" date="2026-11-23">
        <outline text="![Smith Corona Viceroy Typewriter](/images/2026/11/image-23200432.webp)" created="Mon, 23 Nov 2026 20:03:52 GMT"/>
        <outline text="Long ago I used to enjoy finding christmas gifts for people. Now I wish we didn't give each other things. That's not entirely true, I do like giving and receiving presents but I feel like I don't have enough time to do it properly, and end up getting things &quot;that'll do&quot;. " created="Mon, 23 Nov 2026 20:04:34 GMT"/>
        <outline text="I've been thinking about making my own notebooks, and should really investigate it more. That's the sort of thing I'd like to give to people for Christmas - unique notebooks that I've made especially for them." created="Mon, 23 Nov 2026 20:06:55 GMT"/>
        <outline text="Also, I want to buy a X100VI and sell all my other digital cameras and lenses." created="Mon, 23 Nov 2026 20:07:38 GMT"/>
        <outline text="I've been looking at getting a new iPhone for a while, well a refurb older model. I have an alert on hotukdeals for iPhone 17 - I don't know why because no matter how *good* the deal is, it's still £1000 for a phone. Costco has the MBA M5 16GB 512GB model for £1000, which is nice but I also don't need it. Maybe if a 16 Pro gets down to £500 used I'll get one...still too much tbh...perhaps I'll wait another year." created="Mon, 23 Nov 2026 20:09:15 GMT"/>
        <outline text="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=C-TY_XSMboY" created="Mon, 23 Nov 2026 21:15:22 GMT">
          <outline text="Here's me doing a little [POTA](https://pota.app) activation near home."/>
        </outline>
        <outline text="Porridge Updates 🥣" created="Mon, 23 Nov 2026 21:26:41 GMT" list="bullets">
          <outline text="Added YouTube embedding to Porridge, just paste in a youtube URL on it's own line." created="Mon, 23 Nov 2026 21:26:55 GMT"/>
          <outline text="Fiddled with padding and margins - it's a bit like the opticians when they say is it better with lens one or two....three or four... 🤷‍♂️"/>
          <outline text="Under the settings menu you can now customise the site's colours. There are a few presets that the computer decided upon or you can go wild with whatever you want."/>
        </outline>
      </outline>
      <outline text="22nd November" type="calendarDay" date="2026-11-22">
        <outline text="![Fred and his new water fountain](/images/2026/11/img-5553-22095121.jpg)" created="Sun, 22 Nov 2026 09:50:58 GMT"/>
        <outline text="Happy Birthday Fred and Lola 🐈🐈‍⬛" created="Sun, 22 Nov 2026 09:51:26 GMT"/>
        <outline text="I keep thinking a tap is running with this new water fountain of theirs. One cat has drunk from it. The kids want to mess about with it otherwise. " created="Sun, 22 Nov 2026 19:33:36 GMT"/>
        <outline text="More Claude ✳️" created="Sun, 22 Nov 2026 19:36:20 GMT">
          <outline text="Been doing some more updates to my SOTA planner tool. Added activation zone from lidar data or calculated from contour lines. Added a Goals section, so I can group hills by what I want to do. Plus a few bug fixes here and there. " created="Sun, 22 Nov 2026 19:34:27 GMT"/>
          <outline text="![SOTA Planner web app](/images/2026/11/33b2d67b-ccb3-429a-a17f-279fc684c45e-22193811.jpg)"/>
          <outline text="I'd found a tool [someone else made](https://sotaplanner.com/index.php) which does a similar thing to mine. I thought about just using it but it's missing somethings I want and I can just edit mine (with Claude) and add stuff I like from it. That's where I got the goals idea from. "/>
          <outline text="I think I'll investigate being able to download routes from other places, like walkhighlands or maybe be able to display multiple routes at once? Sometimes someone else's route is mostly fine but I want to tweak it. "/>
        </outline>
      </outline>
      <outline text="21st November" type="calendarDay" date="2026-11-21">
        <outline text="![Loch Lomond](/images/2026/11/000009360001-21201545.webp)" created="Sat, 21 Nov 2026 20:15:14 GMT"/>
        <outline text="A new fountain pen 🖋️" created="Sat, 21 Nov 2026 18:31:29 GMT">
          <outline text="Instead of debating endlessly for a week or more, I just went ahead and ordered one, plus some de atramentis document ink for it. Because that's what the lady said she used and it looked good. " created="Sat, 21 Nov 2026 13:51:11 GMT"/>
          <outline text="I'm not sure what the behaviour is if I nest this under an image? Also I don't think the site CSS does much with very deep nestings. At some point I'd like some to actually be a bullet list but not sure how I should trigger that? Perhaps an option in the parent node? "/>
          <outline text="Buying this pen triggered getting a 15% off voucher...maybe I need a mechanical pencil..." created="Sat, 21 Nov 2026 13:57:55 GMT"/>
        </outline>
        <outline text="Porridge updates 🥣" created="Sat, 21 Nov 2026 22:20:18 GMT">
          <outline text="You can add bullets now. Click on the parent bullet menu. A little pill appears on the parent row in the editor so you know." created="Sat, 21 Nov 2026 22:20:29 GMT" list="bullets">
            <outline text="We're all children"/>
            <outline text="I'm the favourite"/>
            <outline text="No, I am."/>
          </outline>
          <outline text="Added a button in the menu to open your rendered blog from the editor"/>
          <outline text="New domain - The editor is now &lt;https://porridge.alexjj.com&gt;">
            <outline text=" btw if you want a custom domain, add it under the Github repo Pages settings, then update the blog settings via the editor."/>
          </outline>
          <outline text="I adjusted the getting started info in the repo - hopefully a little clearer should anyone stumble across it (maybe more so once if i push this to my root domain)."/>
          <outline text="Added quotes. Use the `&gt;` and then a new child with the source.">
            <outline text="&gt; This is the finest blogging platform I've every used.">
              <outline text="Everyone, everywhere."/>
            </outline>
          </outline>
        </outline>
      </outline>
      <outline text="20th November" type="calendarDay" date="2026-11-20">
        <outline text="![A Dreich Driesh](/images/2026/11/000004210035-20084123.webp)" created="Fri, 20 Nov 2026 08:40:13 GMT"/>
        <outline text="Waiting for the plumber to come and fix two water leaks...this is also before he continues working on the bathroom that's been out of action for the week. Least he's coming." created="Fri, 20 Nov 2026 08:28:18 GMT"/>
        <outline text="It means a day at home, without work, and not going hill walking - which is a shame as it's a lovely day, cold but blue skies and sunny. Probably there are things I can be doing to fix stuff or plan christmas etc. Do indoor things that I put off. This also risks sitting on the computer and achieving nothing...which is one reason why I like to go out, at least I achieve something and not just waste away the day" created="Fri, 20 Nov 2026 08:28:59 GMT"/>
      </outline>
      <outline text="18th November" type="calendarDay" date="2026-11-18">
        <outline text="Porridge 🥣" created="Wed, 18 Nov 2026 20:26:18 GMT">
          <outline text="Probably a terrible name but it just popped into my head. This is a blogging engine heavily inspired by drummer and dynalist. Everything is an outline and static files. Right now it's all built and running on Github repo, actions and pages. The intent is that there's nothing to host and it's fairly straight forward for others to host." created="Wed, 18 Nov 2026 20:26:32 GMT"/>
          <outline text="There's the main [app repo](https://github.com/alexjj/porridge), which runs the [interface](https://alexjj.github.io/porridge/), a [blog template](https://github.com/alexjj/porridge-blog-template) repo which you use to start off your blog." created="Wed, 18 Nov 2026 21:17:55 GMT"/>
          <outline text="You link the app to your git repo using a fine-grained token (maybe I'll make a &quot;sign in with Github&quot; thing later) - this is just saved in your browser's local storage - and then the app can commit to your repo. Your repo has a github action in it which will build your blog and then be hosted on github pages (assuming you've turned that on). " created="Wed, 18 Nov 2026 21:17:56 GMT"/>
          <outline text="More instructions will come / are in the readme." created="Wed, 18 Nov 2026 21:17:57 GMT"/>
          <outline text="It *should* work nicely on your phone as well..." created="Wed, 18 Nov 2026 21:17:58 GMT"/>
          <outline text="Oh and Claude code built all of this...if that matters." created="Wed, 18 Nov 2026 21:17:59 GMT"/>
        </outline>
        <outline text="![a big stack of notebooks](/images/2026/11/notebooks-18201150.jpg)" created="Wed, 18 Nov 2026 20:08:28 GMT"/>
        <outline text="Here we are. The first test entry on this new blogging system (not copied, honestly...)" created="Wed, 18 Nov 2026 18:45:38 GMT"/>
      </outline>
    </outline>
  </body>
</opml>
